# Allowlist build context. The image needs only the two Python packages, the
# packaging metadata (NOTICE included: pyproject declares it in license-files,
# so the build fails without it), and -- for air-gapped builds -- ./wheelhouse.
# Everything else in a working tree, local state (demo-state/, *.db, audit
# logs), editor config, tests, node_modules and virtualenvs among it, must
# never be baked into an image. Add a path here deliberately, not by default.
#
# The demo image has its own, wider context: demo/Dockerfile.dockerignore.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE*
!NOTICE
!vecshield/
!vecshield_platform/
!wheelhouse/

# The console is served from the hand-written dist/ bundle; the dashboard's
# tests and Node tooling are not part of the image.
vecshield_platform/api/dashboard/*
!vecshield_platform/api/dashboard/dist/

# Never ship dependencies, caches, build output or state from inside the
# allowed trees (these rules come last so they override the allowlist).
**/node_modules
**/.venv*
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/build
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/demo-state
**/*.db*
**/*.sqlite*
**/*.jsonl
**/*.state
**/.env*
